  "id": "trading_post",
  "kind": "building",
  "notes": "Trading Post (6×9, D-054; water-edge: the back three rows, -y, stand over the sea): a stone quay on the 6×6 land part carrying the kontor barn (bevelled plinth, walls, steep overhanging roof, big doors) and goods, a parked cart at the cart point by the road, and a broad plank pier on piles over the three water rows with the KayKit docks along its front and four mooring piles at the berth slots (berth_1–4). Level 1: timber barn under thatch. Level 2: stone ground floor and plaster under terracotta, a lean-to and a loading crane. Level 3: a pier crane. Level 4: a flag mast.",
